<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- "Ring of days" (AND-34). Twelve marks on a ring: the first three are a
     logged period, the other nine are the rest of a cycle.

     Drawn on the 108-unit adaptive canvas. Every mark is inside 28 units of
     the centre, well within the 72-unit safe zone, so no launcher mask - round,
     squircle, teardrop - can clip any of it.

     The colours are resources rather than literals so values-night can restate
     them: a launcher that honours dark mode gets the dark palette, and one that
     does not gets the light one, which is correct either way.

     Generated geometry, not hand-drawn: twelve dots at radius 23 from (54,54),
     starting at -90 degrees and stepping 30. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
